iio: adc: cf_axi_adc_core: don't swallow debugfs reg_access errors

axiadc_reg_access() computes `ret` from either the converter's
reg_access() callback (SPI-side register access, taken when the
DEBUGFS_DRA_PCORE_REG_MAGIC bit is clear) or the direct PCore MMIO
path (magic bit set), but then unconditionally does `return 0`
instead of `return ret`. Any error from the converter path
(-ENODEV when conv->reg_access is unset, -EINVAL from an IS_ERR
converter, or a converter-specific error) is discarded, and the IIO
debugfs core (industrialio-core.c: iio_debugfs_read_reg/write_reg)
treats the access as successful. On read, this surfaces as a
silent 0x0 instead of an error, which is indistinguishable from a
real all-zero register value on /sys/kernel/debug/iio/iio:deviceX/
direct_reg_access.

Confirmed present upstream at HEAD (analogdevicesinc/linux main,
same file, same bug) as of this writing -- no upstream fix exists
to cherry-pick, so this is authored directly against our pinned
kernel commit.

--- a/drivers/iio/adc/cf_axi_adc_core.c
+++ b/drivers/iio/adc/cf_axi_adc_core.c
@@ -256,7 +256,7 @@ static int axiadc_reg_access(struct iio_dev *indio_dev,
 	}
 	mutex_unlock(&conv->lock);

-	return 0;
+	return ret;
 }

 static int axiadc_decimation_set(struct axiadc_state *st,
